"{\n  \"threat_severity\" : \"Important\",\n  \"public_date\" : \"2026-10-30T11:30:39Z\",\n  \"bugzilla\" : {\n    \"description\" : \"sqlite: sqlite: Denial of service via heap-based buffer overflow in FTS5\",\n    \"id\" : \"2563953\",\n    \"url\" : \"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2563953\"\n  },\n  \"cvss3\" : {\n    \"cvss3_base_score\" : \"7.8\",\n    \"cvss3_scoring_vector\" : \"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H\",\n    \"status\" : \"verified\"\n  },\n  \"cwe\" : \"CWE-787\",\n  \"details\" : [ \"SQLite before 3.54.0 built with FTS5 contains a heap buffer overflow in fts5MergeRowidLists() that undersizes the output buffer when merging detail=none prefix doclists. Attackers who can populate a detail=none FTS5 table with negative rowids and run a prefix MATCH query can write past the allocation, corrupting heap memory and crashing the process.\", \"A flaw was found in SQLite. A heap-based buffer overflow exists in the Full-Text Search 5 (FTS5) extension during the merging of prefix document lists. An attacker capable of inserting negative row identifiers into a configured table and executing a prefix search query can cause data to be written beyond allocated memory. This issue can lead to memory corruption, resulting in application crashes, a Denial of Service (DoS), or potentially arbitrary code execution.\" ],\n  \"affected_release\" : [ {\n    \"product_name\" : \"Red Hat Hardened Images\",\n    \"release_date\" : \"2026-10-20T00:00:00Z\",\n    \"advisory\" : \"RHSA-2026:86202\",\n    \"cpe\" : \"cpe:/a:redhat:hummingbird:1\",\n    \"package\" : \"sqlite-main-3.54.1-1.hum1\"\n  } ],\n  \"package_state\" : [ {\n    \"product_name\" : \"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10\",\n    \"fix_state\" : \"Affected\",\n    \"package_name\" : \"sqlite\",\n    \"cpe\" : \"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:10\"\n  }, {\n    \"product_name\" : \"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 6\",\n    \"fix_state\" : \"Affected\",\n    \"package_name\" : \"sqlite\",\n    \"cpe\" 